\begin_layout Paragraph
Spectral norm of random matrices with independent entries.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An important family of random matrices that merits special attention comprises the ones with independent random entries. We record a spectral norm tail bound for this family, which is of significant utility and is tighter than what matrix Bernstein has to offer. 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
begin{theorem}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "thm:tighter-spectral-normal-ramon"

\end_inset

 Consider a symmetric random matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{X}=[X_{i,j}]_{1\leq i,j\leq n}$
\end_inset

 in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}$
\end_inset

, whose entries are independently generated and obey 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align}
		\label{eq:Xij-condition-iid}
		\mathbb{E}[X_{i,j}]=0 \quad \text{and} \quad  |X_{i,j}|\leq B,  \qquad 1\leq i,j\leq n. 
	\end{align}
\end_inset

Define 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align}
		\label{eq:Xij-row-sum-variance}
		\nu \coloneqq \max_i \sqrt{\sum\nolimits_j \mathbb{E}[X_{i,j}^2]}. 
	\end{align}
\end_inset

Then there is some universal constant 
\begin_inset Formula $c>0$
\end_inset

 such that for any 
\begin_inset Formula $t\geq 0$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align}
		\mathbb{P}\Big\{ \|\bm{X}\|\geq4\sqrt{\nu}+t \Big\} \leq n\exp\Big(-\frac{t^{2}}{cB^{2}}\Big).		
	\end{align}
\end_inset


\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
end{theorem}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This result, which appeared in 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
citep[Remark 3.13]{bandeira2016sharp}
\end_layout

\end_inset

, can be established via tighter control of the expected spectral norm as well as Talagrand's concentration inequality. As a remark, if we know 
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
{
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
em
\end_layout

\end_inset

 a priori
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 that 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{E}[X_{i,j}^2]\leq \sigma^2$
\end_inset

 for all 
\begin_inset Formula $(i,j)$
\end_inset

, then Theorem
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "thm:tighter-spectral-normal-ramon"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

 implies the existence of some constant 
\begin_inset Formula $c_{\mathsf{b}}>0$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align}
	\|\bm{X}\| \leq 4\sigma \sqrt{n} + c_{\mathsf{b}} B \sqrt{ \log n }
	\label{eq:X-spectral-norm-iid-special-ramon}
\end{align}
\end_inset

holds with probability at least 
\begin_inset Formula $1-n^{-8}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

