\end_inset

By definition, 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{U}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{V}^{\top}$
\end_inset

 is the best rank-
\begin_inset Formula $r$
\end_inset

 approximation to 
\begin_inset Formula $p^{-1}\mathcal{P}_{\Omega}(\bm{M}^{\star})$
\end_inset

, i.e.
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{U}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{V}^{\top}-p^{-1}\mathcal{P}_{\Omega}(\bm{M}^{\star})\|=\min_{\bm{A}:\mathsf{rank}(\bm{A})\leq r}\|\bm{A}-p^{-1}\mathcal{P}_{\Omega}(\bm{M}^{\star})\|$
\end_inset

. As a consequence, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align*}
\|\bm{U}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{V}^{\top}-\bm{M}^{\star}\| &\leq\|\bm{U}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{V}^{\top}-p^{-1}\mathcal{P}_{\Omega}(\bm{M}^{\star})\|+\|p^{-1}\mathcal{P}_{\Omega}(\bm{M}^{\star})-\bm{M}^{\star}\| \\ 
