First, the maximum row norm 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{M}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}$
\end_inset

 of 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{M}^{\star}$
\end_inset

 cannot be two large, i.e. 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\|\bm{M}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}=\|\bm{U}^{\star}\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\bm{V}^{\star\top}\|_{2,\infty}\leq\|\bm{U}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\|\|\bm{V}^{\star}\|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\mu r}{n_{1}}}\sigma_{1}(\bm{M}^{\star}),\label{eq:mc-row-norm-upper}
\end{equation}
\end_inset

where the first inequality arises from the elementary inequalities 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{A}\bm{B}\|_{2,\infty}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{B}\|$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{A}\bm{B}\|\leq\|\bm{A}\|\|\bm{B}\|$
\end_inset

. The last relation uses the incoherence assumption on 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{M}^{\star}$
\end_inset

, the orthogonality of 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{V}^{\star}$
\end_inset

, and identifies 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\|$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{1}(\bm{M}^{\star})$
\end_inset

. An analogous upper bound holds for 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{M}^{\star\top}\|_{2,\infty}$
\end_inset

: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\|\bm{M}^{\star\top}\|_{2,\infty}=\|\bm{V}^{\star}\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\bm{U}^{\star\top}\|_{2,\infty}\leq\|\bm{V}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\|\|\bm{U}^{\star}\|\leq\sqrt{\frac{\mu r}{n_{2}}}\sigma_{1}(\bm{M}^{\star}).\label{eq:mc-column-norm-upper}
\end{equation}
\end_inset

In addition, the matrix 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{M}^{\star}$
\end_inset

 is element-wise bounded in the sense that 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\|\bm{M}^{\star}\|_{\infty}=\|\bm{U}^{\star}\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\bm{V}^{\star\top}\|_{\infty}\leq\|\bm{U}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\|\|\bm{V}^{\star}\|_{2,\infty}\leq\frac{\mu r}{\sqrt{n_{1}n_{2}}}\sigma_{1}(\bm{M}^{\star}).\label{eq:mc-entry-upper}
\end{equation}
\end_inset

Here, the first inequality follows from the relation 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{A}\bm{B}^{\top}\|_{\infty}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{B}\|_{2,\infty}$
\end_inset

 and the aforementioned 
\begin_inset Formula $\|\bm{A}\bm{B}\|_{2,\infty}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2,\infty}\|\bm{B}\|$
\end_inset

, while the last one again utilizes the incoherence assumption. 
